    id: "2024-ford-mustang-gt",
    identity: {"year":2024,"make":"Ford","model":"Mustang","trim":"GT Fastback (5.0L V8, 6-speed manual)","bodyClass":"coupe"},
    curbWeightLb: {"value":3730,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted by a third party)","url":"https://ffperformance.co/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/2024-mustang-technical-specifications.pdf","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier card research (2026-11-11). Search summaries of Ford's 2024 Mustang technical specifications PDF said the GT column gives an estimated curb weight of 3,730 lb for the fastback with the manual (3,752 lb with the automatic). WEAK: the sheet is marked preliminary (as of Sept. 14, 2022, subject to change) and the weight is an estimate; one card reviewer said the summary assigned the figure to the GT column by inference from column order; both URLs are third-party re-hosts of the same Ford PDF, so the corroborating URL is the same document, not a second source; the summary did not say whether the figure excludes the GT Performance Package. Kept as the only maker figure that names this body and transmission; both card reviewers recommended caution. Other published weights run 11 to 217 lb higher; see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    weightDistFrontPct: {"value":55,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Motor1 (reporting an LMR weigh-in)","url":"https://www.motor1.com/news/686430/2024-ford-mustang-gt/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"TRANSMISSION MISMATCH: Motor1's article on LMR's scale weigh-in of a 2024 Mustang GT was summarised as 'a 55/45 split' front to rear, but that car had the 10-speed automatic, the 400A package and Brembo brakes, with about three-quarters of a tank of fuel; it is not the manual. Motor Matchup's 2026 GT Fastback Manual listing gives '55.0% front and 45.0% rear' (different model year; not said whether measured or calculated). No Ford figure and no measured split for a 2024 manual surfaced. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    wheelbaseIn: {"value":107,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"The search summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 Mustang spec sheet (forum-hosted PDF) gave the GT a '107-inch wheelbase'. The sheet is marked preliminary (dated Sept. 14, 2022 per the earlier card research) and this copy is a third-party re-host, not Ford's media site. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    trackFrontIn: {"value":62,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 sheet: 'Track width, front 62 62 62.2' with 'the GT column as the middle figure', i.e. 62 in for the GT (62.2 in matches the Dark Horse). Column assignment is the summariser's reading of the table, not a labelled cell. Ford's 2026 sheet gives 62.4 in; see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    trackRearIn: {"value":64.7,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 sheet: 'Track is listed at 62 inches front and 64.7 inches rear' for the GT. Ford's 2026 sheet gives 64.9 in and CarExpert NZ 63.9 in (said to match the Dark Horse column); see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    lengthIn: {"value":189.4,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 sheet: '189.4-inch overall length' for the GT. CarsGuide's 4,789 mm Australian figure was said to match the EcoBoost and was not used. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    widthIn: {"value":75.4,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 sheet: '75.4-inch width without mirrors (81.9 with mirrors)'. CarExpert NZ's 2024 GT Fastback page also gives 75.4 in without mirrors. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    heightIn: {"value":55,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2024 Mustang Technical Specifications, preliminary; copy hosted on a Mustang owners' forum)","url":"https://www.mustang7g.com/forums/attachments/2024-mustang-technical-specifications-pdf.557718","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Summary of Ford's preliminary 2024 sheet: 'Overall height, fastback 55 55 55.2' with the GT column as the middle figure, i.e. 55 in (the summary also called it 'about 55-inch'). CarExpert NZ gives 55.7 in; see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
