    cylinders: {"value":8,"source":{"kind":"agency","name":"U.S. EPA / DOE (fueleconomy.gov)","url":"https://fueleconomy.gov/feg/noframes/47558.shtml","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier card research (2026-11-11). fueleconomy.gov record 47558 was summarised as '8 cylinders, 5.0 liters, manual 6-speed'; confirmed by the card reviewer. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    horsepower: {"value":480,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (From the Road newsroom)","url":"https://www.fromtheroad.ford.com/us/en/articles/2023/all-new-2024-ford-mustang-gt-ready-to-hit-the-track-as-pace-car","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier card research (2026-11-11). Ford's release was summarised as rating the standard Mustang GT at 480 horsepower, with 486 hp only on GT models with the optional active-valve performance exhaust. The card reviewer's TFLcar result agreed (480 standard, 486 with the active exhaust). 480 kept because this configuration names no exhaust option; see conflicts. No rpm for peak power was given. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    horsepowerRpm: {"value":7150,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Ford Motor Company (2026 Mustang Technical Specs)","url":"https://www.fromtheroad.ford.com/content/dam/fordmediasite/us/en/library/2026/specs/2026_Mustang_Technical_Specs.pdf","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"YEAR MISMATCH: the summary said 'Ford's spec sheet gives the GT's peak power at 7,150 rpm and the active exhaust version's at 7,250 rpm', and that the Ford document found was the 2026 Mustang sheet, whose 480 hp / 415 lb-ft ratings match the 2024 GT. No 2024 Ford figure was seen. mustangspecs.com gives 7,500 rpm; see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    torqueLbFt: {"value":415,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Jalopnik (reporting Ford's SAE figures)","url":"https://jalopnik.com/2024-ford-mustang-gt-ecoboost-manual-specs-photos-info-1849534613","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier card research (2026-11-11). Jalopnik was summarised as reporting Ford's figures: 480 hp and 415 lb-ft for the GT without the active-valve exhaust, 486 hp and 418 lb-ft with it. The card reviewer's TFLcar result agreed and said the ratings are the same for the manual and the 10-speed automatic. Ford's own newsroom summary printed only the 418 lb-ft (active exhaust) figure, so the 415 figure is republished, not read on a Ford page. URL is the Jalopnik slug the reviewer saw for article id 1849534613. No rpm for peak torque was given. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
