    curbWeightLb: {"value":4604,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"The Drive","url":"https://www.thedrive.com/car-reviews/2024-jeep-wrangler-first-drive-review-specs-price-options-impressions","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Copied from earlier card research: The Drive's 2024 first-drive review lists its four-door Rubicon with the 3.6 V6 and eight-speed automatic at 4,604 lb; auto-data.net gives 2,088 kg (4,603 lb) for the JL facelift Unlimited Rubicon 3.6 automatic. A JL Wrangler Forums post on official 2024 curb weights says the V6 manual is 29 lb lighter than the V6 automatic, which matches the 4,575 lb that J.D. Power and Auto123 give for the Rubicon 4-door V6 6-speed manual. Earlier reviewers did not reproduce 4,604 lb in their own searches; Jeep's own FAQ gives only a 4,287-4,976 lb range for all four-door Wranglers (see conflicts). Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
