    gearRatios: {"value":[4.89,3.17,2.15,1.56,1.18,0.94,0.76,0.61],"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Porsche (2020 911 Carrera S and Carrera 4S US specifications)","url":"https://newsroom.porsche.com:443/dam/jcr:d5712d5c-b376-41d9-8201-09731162e143/2020_911_Carrera_S_and_911_Carrera_4S_US_specifications.pdf.PDF","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"TRIM CAUTION. The summary of Porsche's 2020 US sheet for the base 911 Carrera showed 'Transmission: Number of gears 8 ... 1st 4.89 4.89, 2nd 3.17 3.17' and was cut off after second gear. The full set (3rd 2.15, 4th 1.56, 5th 1.18, 6th 0.94, 7th 0.76, 8th 0.61, reverse 3.99) came from Porsche's 2020 Carrera S / Carrera 4S US sheet. The same eight ratios appeared on Stuttcars listings for a Carrera 4S PDK, a Carrera 4S Cabriolet and a 992.2 Carrera S. Third to eighth gear were therefore not seen for the base Carrera itself; they are recorded because the base sheet's first and second gears match and every 992 8-speed PDK listing seen carried the same ratios. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    finalDriveRatio: {"value":3.39,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Porsche (2020 911 Carrera US specifications)","url":"https://download.newsroom.porsche.com/dam/jcr:683ce58d-5a57-4bd0-bf5f-b1bf5fe1931d/2020_911_Carrera_and_911_Carrera_Cabriolet_US_specifications.pdf","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Added by the second reader. A search summary said: 'Porsche's US spec sheet for the 2020 Carrera and Cabriolet lists 2.15 for third and 0.61 for eighth, alongside a 3.39 rear axle ratio and 0.92 rear constant transaxle ratio', and 'Porsche's sheet for the 2020 Carrera S and 4S reports the same 3.39 rear axle ratio. Rear Axle Ratio / rear constant transaxle ratio 3.39 / 0.92'. Model year 2020 base Carrera (992.1, the same 8-speed PDK car as the 2024). CAUTION: the sheet prints two numbers, a 3.39 rear axle ratio and a 0.92 'rear constant transaxle ratio'. No summary said whether the overall reduction is 3.39 alone or 3.39 with the 0.92 stage applied; the product is deliberately not recorded. 3.56 on Stuttcars is the manual gearbox (Carrera 4S Cabriolet), not the PDK. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
