    awdKind: null,
    transmissionType: {"value":"cvt","source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Subaru of America (media.subaru.com)","url":"https://media.subaru.com/pressrelease/2020/1/subaru-announces-pricing-2024-outback-legacy-models","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier card research (engine/data/research/batch-2-2026-11-11.json); no search in the 2026-11-24 pass was spent on this figure. Subaru's 2024 Outback pricing release: the naturally aspirated engine is paired with a standard Lineartronic CVT that includes an 8-speed manual shift mode (paddle shift switches). EPA transmission code AV-S8 (variable, 8 selectable ratios). The CVT's ratio range is recorded under gearRatios from Subaru Europe's 2024 sheet; only manual-mode steps 5-8 were seen, so gearCount is left blank. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    gearRatios: {"value":[4.066,0.503],"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Subaru Europe (2024 Outback specification sheet)","url":"https://www.subaru.eu/docs/default-source/media-documents-gallery/spec-sheets/24outback_spec_ec.pdf","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"CVT, so these are the two ends of the ratio range, lowest (launch) ratio first, not discrete gears. MARKET MISMATCH: Subaru's European 2024 Outback sheet (2.5i Limited and Field) was summarised as 'Lineartronic D range of 4.066 - 0.503, a reverse of 4.379, and a final drive axle ratio 3.900'; a second summary of the same sheet gave manual-mode steps 5th 1.166, 6th 0.914, 7th 0.717, 8th 0.559 (1st-4th not shown). No US sheet giving the range surfaced. auto123's 2024 Limited and Touring listings (Canadian 2.5) give '4.07 - 0.84', reverse 4.38 - the 4.07 low end agrees, the 0.84 top end does not (see conflicts). Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    finalDriveRatio: {"value":3.9,"source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Subaru Europe (2024 Outback specification sheet)","url":"https://www.subaru.eu/docs/default-source/media-documents-gallery/spec-sheets/24outback_spec_ec.pdf","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"MARKET MISMATCH: Subaru's European 2024 Outback sheet lists 'final drive axle ratio 3.900' (with reverse 4.379); a second Subaru 2024 sheet hosted at fernandesautomotive.com gave the same final drive and reverse. auto123's 2024 Limited and Touring listings (Canadian market, same 2.5 Lineartronic as the US) give a 3.90 final drive axle ratio. The 4.111 figure is from Subaru's 2026 US sheet (next-generation car); see conflicts. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    diffFront: null,
