    gearRatios: {"value":[5.25,3.03,1.95,1.46,1.22,1,0.81,0.67],"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Motor Matchup","url":"https://www.motormatchup.com/catalog/Toyota/Camry/2024/SE-Auto-(Natl)","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Search summary for the 2024 Camry 2.5L with the 8-speed automatic: Motor Matchup's gear table gives 'Gear Ratios 1: 5.25 ... 8: 0.67' (5.25, 3.03, 1.95, 1.46, 1.22, 1.00, 0.81, 0.67), reverse 4.01; 'Auto123 and TrueCar match these for the first four gears and the upper gears'. The summary did not say which Motor Matchup 2024 Camry listing held the table (the results were SE Auto (Natl), XLE Auto (GS) and two AWD listings), and the Auto123 corroboration is its 2024 SE listing, which shares the LE's 203-hp 2.5L/8-speed/FWD driveline; no LE-specific or Toyota ratio table was seen. Yahoo's buyer's guide mislabels 3.03 as reverse. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    finalDriveRatio: {"value":2.802,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"TrueCar","url":"https://www.truecar.com/toyota/camry/2019/specs/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Second reader's search summary: 'TrueCar's spec pages for the 2019 Camry list a 5.25 first-gear ratio and a 2.802 final drive axle ratio, with eight gears' ('Gear Number 8, Final Drive Axle Ratio 2.802, First Gear Ratio 5.25'). The results held two TrueCar 2019 Camry pages (L Automatic and SE Automatic) and the summary did not say which carried the line; both are the same-generation four-cylinder car, and the 5.25 first gear ties the figure to the 2.5L's UB80E gear set recorded in gearRatios. A 2019 listing, not a 2024 one, and a third-party aggregator, not a Toyota figure. Replaces the first reader's 2.8, whose only attributable source was Motor Matchup's 2024 SE Nightshade AWD listing (https://www.motormatchup.com/catalog/Toyota/Camry/2024/SE-Nightshade-Auto-AWD-(GS)), a different drivetrain, alongside an unattributed 'Final Drive Axle Ratio 2.802' that this search now attributes to TrueCar. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
