    transmissionType: {"value":"automatic","source":{"kind":"manufacturer","name":"Toyota USA Newsroom","url":"https://pressroom.toyota.com/2024-toyota-rav4-go-wild-in-style/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Copied from the card research (engine/data/research/batch-2-2026-11-11.json). Toyota describes the gas-grade transmission as a Direct Shift 8-speed automatic that locks up in gears two through eight, a torque-converter automatic, stated for all gas grades. The checker's EPA-derived row reads 'Automatic (S8)'. This pass's search also saw the brochure wording 'Direct Shift 8-speed Automatic Transmission' for the non-hybrid 2.5L. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    gearRatios: {"value":[5.25,3.03,1.95,1.46,1.22,1,0.81,0.67],"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Auto123","url":"https://www.auto123.com/en/specs/toyota/rav4/toyota-rav4-2024-xle-ti-445213/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"The search summary for the 2024 RAV4 2.5L 8-speed gave 'First Gear Ratio (:1): 5.25 ... Second 3.03 ... Third 1.95 ... Fourth 1.46 ... Fifth 1.22 ... Sixth 1.00 ... Seventh 0.81 ... Eighth 0.67' (reverse 4.01) from the Auto123 2024 listings (XLE, Trail, Limited, LE among the results; the summary did not pin each ratio to the XLE page specifically). Auto123 is a Canadian site; its 2024 RAV4 'XLE' listing (its EPA class is shown as a 4WD small SUV; the URL slug 'xle-ti' is read as the French 'traction integrale') is the AWD XLE, but the search summary did not show its drivetrain field, and it may carry Canadian-market data. No Toyota spec sheet with the ratios surfaced; the summary called these third-party database values. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    finalDriveRatio: {"value":3.18,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Auto123","url":"https://www.auto123.com/en/specs/toyota/rav4/toyota-rav4-2024-xle-ti-445213/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Auto123's 2024 RAV4 XLE and Trail listings give 'Final Drive Axle Ratio (:1): 3.18'; Motor Matchup's 2024 AWD and FWD pages also list 'Final Drive: 3.18'; TrueCar's 2020 Limited AWD lists 3.177, the same value at higher precision. The 2.5L hybrid's 3.605 is a different powertrain. Auto123 is a Canadian site; its 2024 RAV4 'XLE' listing (its EPA class is shown as a 4WD small SUV; the URL slug 'xle-ti' is read as the French 'traction integrale') is the AWD XLE, but the search summary did not show its drivetrain field, and it may carry Canadian-market data.  Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
