    wheelbaseIn: {"value":131.9,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Toyota (2024 Tacoma product information sheet, copy hosted on Tacoma4G forum)","url":"https://www.tacoma4g.com/forum/attachments/2024_toyota_tacoma_product_information-pdf.12235","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Toyota's product information sheet gives the 4x4 Double Cab table as 'wheelbase of 145.1 in. and 131.9 in.'; 131.9 in is the 5-ft bed and 145.1 in the 6-ft bed. This record assumes the 5-ft bed (the bed of the Car and Driver test truck per 0-60specs, and of the Edmunds TRD Off-Road automatic listing). CarSpecs' 2024 TRD Off-Road Double Cab 5' Bed listing also gives '131.90 in. Wheelbase'. Toyota document re-hosted on a forum, so marked republished. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    trackFrontIn: {"value":66,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Toyota (2024 Tacoma product information sheet, copy hosted on Tacoma4G forum)","url":"https://www.tacoma4g.com/forum/attachments/2024_toyota_tacoma_product_information-pdf.12235","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"The sheet lists front and rear tread of 65.6, 66.0 or 66.9 in depending on wheel and tire package, and its footnotes tie 66.0 in to the 265/70R17 tires on the Off-Road grade. The summary warned the table layout makes the row-to-value mapping hard to verify, so treat as probable rather than certain. Velocity Journal's generic 2024 Double Cab entry gives 65.6 in (see conflicts). Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    trackRearIn: {"value":66,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Toyota (2024 Tacoma product information sheet, copy hosted on Tacoma4G forum)","url":"https://www.tacoma4g.com/forum/attachments/2024_toyota_tacoma_product_information-pdf.12235","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Same sheet and footnote as trackFrontIn: front and rear tread both 66.0 in with the Off-Road grade's 265/70R17 tires; 65.6 in and 66.9 in belong to other wheel/tire packages. Row-to-value mapping flagged as hard to verify in the summary. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    lengthIn: {"value":213,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"CarSpecs.us","url":"https://www.carspecs.us/cars/2024/toyota/tacoma/99055","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"CarSpecs' listing for the 2024 TRD Off-Road Double Cab 5' Bed (the manual-transmission listing; body is the same as the automatic) reads '213.00 in. Length, 77.90 Width, 74.50 in. Height, 131.90 in. Wheelbase'. The search returned two CarSpecs 2024 Tacoma pages (ids 99055 and 98704) and the summary did not say which one held these figures. No Toyota length figure surfaced. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    widthIn: {"value":77.9,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"CarSpecs.us","url":"https://www.carspecs.us/cars/2024/toyota/tacoma/99055","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"CarSpecs' 2024 TRD Off-Road Double Cab 5' Bed listing: '77.90 Width'. Whether this excludes mirrors was not stated. Same page-id caveat as lengthIn (99055 or 98704). Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    heightIn: {"value":74.5,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"CarSpecs.us","url":"https://www.carspecs.us/cars/2024/toyota/tacoma/99055","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"CarSpecs' 2024 TRD Off-Road Double Cab 5' Bed listing: '74.50 in. Height'. Edmunds' 2025 TRD Off-Road page gives 73.9 in (different model year; see conflicts). Same page-id caveat as lengthIn. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    groundClearanceIn: {"value":11,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Toyota (2024 Tacoma product information sheet, copy hosted on Tacoma4G forum)","url":"https://www.tacoma4g.com/forum/attachments/2024_toyota_tacoma_product_information-pdf.7063","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Carried over from the earlier trading-card research record (engine/data/research/batch-2-2026-11-11.json, checked 'confirmed' against a second forum-hosted copy of the same sheet, .12235): 11.0 in running clearance for the TRD Off-Road grade, with 32.5 deg approach, 24.7 deg breakover, 26.6 deg departure. Cab, bed and powertrain for that line not stated. Toyota's MY24 overview says 'max running ground clearance up to 10.9 in.' range-wide (see conflicts). Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    cgHeightIn: null,
    powertrain: {"value":"gasoline","source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Performance Plus Tire (Tacoma tire size by trim)","url":"https://www.performanceplustire.com/Blog/tacoma-tire-size-by-trim","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"The tire guide separates '2024-26 TRD Off-Road, i-FORCE gas' from the hybrid; BFGoodrich's fitment pages likewise label the trim 'trd-off-road-gas'. Toyota's overview lists the i-FORCE 2.4L Turbo as the standard engine and the i-FORCE MAX hybrid as the option. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
