    gearRatios: {"value":[4.41,2.81,1.95,1.51,1.27,1,0.79,0.65],"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Auto123","url":"https://www.auto123.com/en/specs/toyota/tacoma/toyota-tacoma-2024-4x4-double-cab-auto-448683/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Auto123's 2024 Tacoma '4x4 Double Cab auto' specs: 'First Gear Ratio (:1): 4.41 Second Gear Ratio (:1): 2.81', third 1.95, fourth 1.51, fifth 1.27, sixth 1.00, 'Seventh Gear Ratio (:1): 0.79', 'Eighth Gear Ratio (:1): 0.65', reverse 3.65. Seventh and eighth were read in one search, third to sixth in another. Toyota's product information sheet (forum-hosted) gives the first three as 4.413, 2.808, 1.950 for the i-FORCE 8-speed, agreeing to two decimals; its fourth to eighth ratios did not appear in any summary. Auto123 is a Canadian listing labelled by cab and drive, not by the TRD Off-Road name. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
    finalDriveRatio: {"value":3.58,"source":{"kind":"reference","name":"Auto123","url":"https://www.auto123.com/en/specs/toyota/tacoma/toyota-tacoma-2024-4x4-double-cab-auto-448683/","asOf":"2026-11-24","note":"Auto123's 2024 Tacoma '4x4 Double Cab auto' page lists 'Axle Ratio (:1) - Front: 3.58' and 3.58 for the rear. Not tied to the TRD Off-Road by name, and no Toyota axle ratio surfaced; the only other figure seen, 3.909, is from TacomaWorld forum posts about the 2016-2023 V6 automatic and does not apply. Read from search-result summary; page not opened."}},
